2	{"type":"hv_request_scope","overallBar":"AGREE only when accuracy and completeness are each >= 98.","primaryAsk":"This is a SCOPED re-review of two small amendments to the R4-AGREE packet. Verify each amendment is internally consistent and introduces no contradiction or regression; then re-adjudicate the affected tasks and the overall verdict. Do not re-litigate the already-AGREE R4 content except to confirm no regression.","changesUnderReview":["B1 provider amendment (architecture section 8 and bdpv4 section 5): records operator decision 2026-11-11 (MEMORY-PREFERENCE-002) that a prerelease or community-fork EF Core 10 MySQL-wire provider, patched by this project and contributed upstream as needed, is an ACCEPTED dependency for the Dolt project context; the earlier GA-maintained-provider bar is relaxed for this engine. A silent EF downgrade and a bespoke from-scratch provider remain forbidden without operator agreement; report alternatives only if no provider can be made to drive Dolt even with reasonable patching.","xUnit v3 test standard (bdpv4 section 4): new federation test projects target xUnit v3 and use native skip (Assert.Skip/SkipWhen/SkipUnless); no Xunit.SkippableFact or v2 xunit packages, per MEMORY-BESTPRACTICE-001 section 10."],"verifyFocus":["The B1 amendment must not contradict: DEPLOY HOLD; the B1-B12 unproven-feasibility gating; the \"no package is installed\" stance; or Ph0 remaining a real go/no-go. Confirm B1 is still a gate (a provider-enablement spike), not an assumption that the provider works.","Confirm the amendment keeps the honest guard: silent EF downgrade and bespoke provider still forbidden; alternatives reported if patching cannot make it work. No claim that feasibility is proven.","The xUnit reference must be consistent: MEMORY-BESTPRACTICE-001 section 10 exists and says xUnit v3 / native skip / no SkippableFact-or-v2; the reference does not contradict any existing test-gate guidance in bdpv4 section 4 or elsewhere.","Regression: confirm the eight R2 findings and the R3/R4 phase-annotation reconciliation remain intact (unchanged by this delta); the error-code mapping, FR-183/FR-184 Ph4 annotations, 91->99 count, already_applied, dispositions D1 are untouched.","Operator decisions U1 (Dolt selected) and U2 (cell-merge accepted) remain recorded and consistent."],"infraRule":"Infrastructure limitations do not force DISAGREE or lower a score (MEMORY-HV-001 section 6). Plan-readiness; unproven B1-B12 are not planning defects.","evidencePaths":["docs/plans/2026-11-10-federation-dolt-architecture.md","docs/plans/2026-11-10-federation-dolt-bdpv4.md","docs/plans/2026-11-10-federation-current-contracts.md","docs/plans/2026-11-10-federation-reconciliation.md","docs/plans/2026-11-10-federation-library-options.md","docs/plans/2026-11-11-federation-correctness-evaluation.md","docs/Project/federation-dolt/Technical-Requirements.md","docs/Project/federation-dolt/Requirements-Matrix.md","docs/receipts/hv/20261111T100429-federation-r4-plan-readiness.verdict.md"],"outputContract":"Return the COMPLETE verdict: overall verdict + accuracy + completeness; a short consistency verdict for each of the two amendments; a regression statement (intact / regressed with detail) for the prior R2-R4 findings; any NEW findings with severity and file:anchor; explicit FAIL and UNKNOWN lists. No table-style formatting; use bullets."}
3

